TEXT -80 8 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}\n.options vntol=1 abstol=100m reltol=0.001
TEXT -80 32 Left 2 !.ac list 59.9 60 60.1
TEXT -128 -16 Left 2 ;One Phase fault: Z=U/I=4.569ohm=Impedance due to selfinductance\nsee also ATP-Matrix
TEXT -104 152 Left 2 ;Z=612.3kV/134kA=4.569ohm
TEXT -104 176 Left 2 ;see line_coupled.lib \nper km reactance matrix (resistance small, not considered)\n+ XL11=4.576542E-01\n+ XM12=1.358979E-01 XL22=4.517972E-01\n+ XM13=9.094776E-02 XM23=1.358979E-01 XL33=4.576542E-01
TEXT -168 168 Left 0 ;CTRL+Line for drawing lines not\nsnapped to grid
TEXT -128 248 Left 2 ;NOTE that phase 2 and phase 3 have overvoltages\nbecause of the coupling to phase1\nThe reactance of phase 1 increase (to the level of selfinductance) \nsince there is no reducing due to mutual inductance of phase 2,3 (current=0)\nThe voltage drop of phase 1, is coupled to the phases 2,3\nand so yield to a higher and asymmetric voltage
TEXT -128 312 Left 2 ;VERY IMPORTANT:\nYou can see with this example that the coupling of the phases is \nvery important by modelling asymmetric faults !!!
TEXT -8 168 Left 1 ;XL11,22,33 self inductances\nXM's mutual inductances between phases
